---
description: Interpret executed contract duties as a relation graph and test observed events against their precise triggers.
args: { request: ObligationReviewRequest; dossier: ContractEvidenceDossier }
returns: ObligationProgramResult
uses: [contractDesk/frameContract, contractDesk/resolvePartyIdentity, contractDesk/bindBusinessCalendar, contractDesk/evaluateEffectiveNotice, contractDesk/branchDisputedClause, contractDesk/minimizeConfidentialInstruction, obligationWorkbench/parseDutyFacets, obligationWorkbench/linkClauseRelations, obligationWorkbench/testEventTriggers, obligationWorkbench/planOwnedPerformance, obligationWorkbench/reconcileDischarge]
---
Bind scope = `frameContract(request, dossier.contracts)`. Bind identity = `resolvePartyIdentity(request, dossier.partyIdentityChanges)`, calendar = `bindBusinessCalendar(request, dossier.businessCalendars)`, notice = `evaluateEffectiveNotice(request, dossier.noticeReceipts)`, disputed = `branchDisputedClause(request, dossier.disputedClauseRefs)`, and confidentiality = `minimizeConfidentialInstruction(request, dossier.confidentialTaskRefs)` as independent findings; none can resolve another by implication.

Bind duties = `parseDutyFacets(scope, dossier.contracts, dossier.evidencePages)` against the exact agreement editions. Keep actor, modality, action, triggering condition, deadline rule, exception and territorial scope as separate facets. A legal-name change does not merge actors unless identity evidence establishes continuity or succession. Bind relations = `linkClauseRelations(duties, dossier.evidencePages)` so depends, excepts, supersedes and conflicts remain explicit edges; do not collapse related duties into one obligation. Preserve competing clause readings from disputed when text supports more than one consequence.

Bind triggers = `testEventTriggers(duties, relations, dossier.evidencePages, notice)` for each observed event. Activate only duties whose specific event facts and contractual notice condition are established. A sent message is not effective notice without the agreement's required delivery and destination evidence. Where deadline rules require business days, use a due date only when calendar contains the incorporated jurisdiction, holidays and timezone; otherwise leave it unknown. Bind tasks = `planOwnedPerformance(request, duties, relations, triggers, calendar, identity)` only for active duties with an identified owner; each task names prerequisites and evidence needed to prove performance. Bind statuses = `reconcileDischarge(duties, triggers, tasks, dossier.evidencePages)` and keep partial, disputed, waived and satisfied states distinct. Return the obligation graph and guardrails with commitAllowed false. Task assignment, confidential disclosure, notice dispatch and legal determinations remain separate authorized effects.